<title>GERMANY: Lamfalussy-Policy mixes to decide Euro-dollar rate.</title>
<headline>Lamfalussy-Policy mixes to decide Euro-dollar rate.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute President Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Monday that the future relationship between the Euro and dollar would depend on a range of policy factors from both sides.</p>
<p>&quot;What will determine the situation with the Euro-dollar relation is the competitive set of policy mixes on both sides, as always,&quot; Lamfalussy said at an evening meeting with journalists.</p>
<p>The EMI president added the dollar's current strength was &quot;the result of a longstanding economic upswing in the United States,&quot; rather than any other factor.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
